    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "Model no3/po4 are stored in mol m-3 while WOA23 is per unit mass, so the requested µmol/kg conversion at 1025 kg/m3 and the N:P and regression results depend on handling units correctly.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `no3` and `po4` are in mol m-3 (per volume), while WOA23 is per mass (µmol kg-1). The ×1e3 prefix change gives mmol m-3, not µmol kg-1. For the regression, scatter and axes, convert with µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ, using the question's constant ρ = 1025 kg m-3, and state that density.",
        "N:P ratios, depths and gradients are scale-invariant: take them from the native fields, since a constant ρ cancels. The slope and R² are also unaffected by the scaling, but the intercept b needs the conversion. Do not label mol m-3 ×1000 as µmol/kg."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The cell-by-cell N:P, regression, volume percentages and N:P-minus-16 maps need one grid and one common valid-cell mask applied to all four sources, since WOA23 and the models cover different cells.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Regrid all four sources to one grid and build one shared mask with `build_comparison_mask`, applied with `.where(mask)` before any metric. Use that sample for the regression and the cell-by-cell comparisons. WOA23 is in the comparison, so the default `ocean_only=True` is appropriate. Build the mask from the fields at the 200-1000 m layer, not from the surface. Report the cell counts.",
        "State that global means over each source's own ocean differ from the shared-sample means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "Basin statistics for Pacific, Atlantic and Indian depend on the partition used, and the question specifies the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded in and Southern and Arctic excluded, which must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use the WOA23 basin mask (`select_basin`, `load_basin_mask`) with marginal seas folded in (`include_marginal_seas=True`). Southern and Arctic are separate basins, excluded here as the question says. State this choice.",
        "The mask labels each level separately. A named ocean over the whole layer means surface labels (`depth_dependent=False`). State which setting was used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Volume-percentage metrics (N:P between 14 and 18, below 12) and volume-based statistics need each model's own volcello weighting over all cells in the 200-1000 m layer.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Volume-weight with `compute_basic_stat` `op='volume_weighted_mean'`, using NaN-aware weights restricted to valid cells and each model's own volcello. The ratio of means is the weighted mean of each field, divided. The mean of the cell-by-cell N:P comes from `compute_ratio`. Label the two clearly, with the cell-by-cell mean as the headline.",
        "The shares of volume with N:P in 14-18 and below 12 are shares of volume, not of cells. Use `compute_exceedance_fraction` with missing cells out of the denominator, and report the volume (m3) next to the percentage. The regression, by the question's definition, weights each cell equally, so it differs from the volume-weighted statistics. State this."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Volume-weighted quantities should be computed on native grids and regridding used only for map display and pattern comparison, which fits the request to regrid curvilinear fields for display only.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the numbers (means, volume shares, basin means) on each source's native grid with its own weights. Regrid only for the maps and the common-mask regression and scatter. State which grid each number comes from and the `regrid_horizontal` method, with 'conservative' before area-weighted steps.",
        "Integrate layers on the original levels to avoid interpolation bias. Do not select the nearest level for 200 and 1000 m."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
