      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI are curvilinear native grids while GFDL-ESM4 is regridded 1° gr with 35 z levels, which affects masks, the layer selection of 200-1000 m, and the map display.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr` (regridded to 1°, 35 z levels), so its \"native\" numbers are on the 1° archive grid with a regridded land-sea mask. CESM2 and MPI are `gn`. Say this when comparing the sources."
      ]
    },
    {
