    {
      "id": "bgc-model-structure-comparison",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "datasets/bgc-model-structure-comparison.md",
      "sha256": "4ef3e4ab0b9741f6ab5d15f88cfbdf8b7366c82b093ce99e26f1707a2a788e54",
      "reason": "Differences in stoichiometry (CESM2 variable C:P, GFDL fixed N:P, MPI Redfield) and in N2 fixation and denitrification help interpret whether the models reproduce the low-N:P denitrification signal.",
      "status": "dropped",
      "notes": [
        "When interpreting the N:P results, note that MPI-ESM1-2-LR (HAMOCC6) uses prescribed Redfield stoichiometry. GFDL has fixed N:P per plankton type, and CESM2 has variable C:P. Model N:P departures therefore reflect N-cycle and transport processes plus model structure. MPI's anaerobic remineralisation on NO3 is described in the paper, so do not infer that any model lacks a denitrification feature."
      ]
